{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFollow-up (fix b) discovered during creatable-foldable-arthropods (fix a, merged as a0fc8d43556 / Gerrit 1761). Fix (a) stopped the runaway-loop guard from counting memo-served repeats as loop evidence. A second, independent defect remains in the completion verifier's evidence-banking path: at SEARCH EXHAUSTION, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` banks `met=false` — i.e. \"the criterion is unmet\" — when what the run actually established is only \"the search budget ran out before sufficient evidence was found\". Banking a hard negative from an exhausted search misattributes absence-of-evidence as evidence-of-absence: subsequent verifier passes (and the close gate) treat the criterion as affirmatively failed, producing false FAIL verdicts on tickets whose evidence exists but was not reached within the window.\n\n## Proposed fix\nMake the banked evidence TRI-STATE: `met=true`, `met=false` (a positive refutation was actually found), and `insufficient_evidence` (search exhausted without a determination). The tri-state must originate in the banking WRITE path, whose chokepoints are all bool-typed today and must each change:\n- `CompletionEvidencePolicy.fallback_record` (completion_tool_policy.py:100-101) currently passes a literal `False` through the record tool — at exhaustion it must bank the `insufficient_evidence` sentinel instead, via an internal write path (not the model-facing tool).\n- `CriterionBank.upsert` (completion_banking.py:441-461) hard-codes `\"met\": bool(met)` at :454 — widen it to accept and persist `bool | \"insufficient_evidence\"` (e.g. `met: bool | None` plus an explicit `state` field, or a sentinel-aware `met`; the docstring's \"writes remain bool-only\" contract updates with it).\n- `record_criterion_verdict`'s model-facing tool signature (:539, `met: bool`) stays BOOL — the model can only assert met/unmet from evidence; `insufficient_evidence` is exclusively the policy-side exhaustion outcome, so the tri-state is not exposed as a model-tool input.\n- `harvest_structured_into_bank` (:583) hard-gates `isinstance(record.get(\"met\"), bool)` and would SILENTLY DROP a tri-state entry on successor re-harvest — widen the gate so `insufficient_evidence` entries survive harvest round-trips.\nAt search exhaustion, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` must bank `insufficient_evidence`, never `met=false`.\n\n**Full consumer graph (all bool-coercing/validating sites change together):**\n- **Schema (`src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json`)**: per-criterion `met` is strict boolean (:31) and top-level `verdict` normalizes to PASS/FAIL (:10-12). Widen: `criteria[].met` becomes `boolean|null` with a sibling optional `state` enum (`met` / `unmet` / `insufficient_evidence`; absent state + bool met keeps full backward compatibility for existing records), and top-level `verdict` gains the `INDETERMINATE` token, emitted when no criterion is `unmet` but at least one is `insufficient_evidence` (any genuine `unmet` still dominates → FAIL). Both rendering seams' outputs validate against this schema (completion_recovery.py:674, :774), so the widening is a prerequisite, not a follow-up.\n- **`_validate_coverage` (completion_recovery.py:364-368, run at :717 on the merged verdict)**: hard-raises on non-bool `met` — widen to accept the tri-state (null met + state field) while still rejecting genuinely untyped records; the `verdict == 'PASS' and any(not record['met'])` cross-check (:370) becomes state-aware (PASS requires all `met`; INDETERMINATE requires no `unmet`).\n- **`_run_finalizer` banked-evidence rendering (completion_recovery.py:741)**: currently `bool(entry.get('met'))` collapses the sentinel to false BEFORE the LLM finalizer sees it — render `insufficient_evidence` faithfully in the finalizer prompt payload instead.\n- **The unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches** in `assemble_deterministic_verdict` (completion_banking.py:646-660) and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` (:715+): a never-banked criterion at budget exhaustion is EXACTLY absence-of-evidence, so those placeholders bank/render `insufficient_evidence` (with the existing `exhausted` marker) instead of `met:false` + high-severity FAIL finding — same treatment as the bounded-search fallback.\n- **Completion sidecar (`src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py:335`)**: persists `criteria` records as-is (no coercion) — verified pass-through; covered by the schema widening, no code change expected (a round-trip test pins this). Both verdict-rendering seams — `assemble_deterministic_verdict` (completion_banking.py:619-640) and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` (:705-714) — must render `insufficient_evidence` as INDETERMINATE, not FAIL. **Close-gate behavior (fail-closed):** an `insufficient_evidence` criterion still BLOCKS the close — the gate does not pass on missing evidence — but the refusal carries the INDETERMINATE remediation messaging (re-run verification, widen the search scope, or operator-attest the criterion) instead of asserting the criterion affirmatively FAILED. The behavioral change is honesty of the message and the recorded verdict class, not gate leniency.\n\n## Scope\n- The banking WRITE path: `fallback_record` wiring in src/rebar/llm/completion_tool_policy.py (exhaustion site), and in src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py: `CriterionBank.upsert` (schema widening), `record_criterion_verdict` (unchanged bool tool signature — guard only), `harvest_structured_into_bank` (gate widening so tri-state entries survive re-harvest), and BOTH unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches (assemble_deterministic_verdict :646-660, merge_finalizer_with_bank :715+).\n- src/rebar/schemas/completion_verdict.schema.json — criteria[].met boolean|null + state enum + INDETERMINATE verdict token (backward compatible).\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py — `_validate_coverage` tri-state acceptance + state-aware PASS/INDETERMINATE cross-check; `_run_finalizer` banked-evidence payload renders the sentinel faithfully (:741).\n- src/rebar/llm/completion_sidecar.py — verified pass-through (round-trip test only; no code change expected).\n- The evidence schema + BOTH consumer seams that render per-criterion verdicts from banked evidence: `assemble_deterministic_verdict` and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` in src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_banking.py.\n- Tests: a search-exhaustion run banks insufficient_evidence (not met=false); a genuine refutation still banks met=false; verdict rendering distinguishes the two.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At search exhaustion, banked fallback evidence is `insufficient_evidence`, not `met=false`; checked by a new unit test.\n- [ ] An `insufficient_evidence` bank entry survives `harvest_structured_into_bank` round-trips (not silently dropped) and the model-facing `record_criterion_verdict` tool signature remains bool-only; unit tests.\n- [ ] A genuine positive refutation still banks `met=false` and still yields FAIL; checked by a guard test.\n- [ ] BOTH rendering seams — `assemble_deterministic_verdict` and `merge_finalizer_with_bank` — render `insufficient_evidence` as indeterminate-with-remediation, not FAIL, INCLUDING their unbanked/exhausted placeholder branches; checked per-seam and per-branch by rendering tests.\n- [ ] The widened completion_verdict schema validates tri-state records and still validates existing all-bool records; `_validate_coverage` accepts the tri-state and still rejects untyped records; `_run_finalizer`'s banked-evidence payload carries the sentinel unconverted; sidecar round-trip preserves the state field; unit tests each.\n- [ ] The close gate still BLOCKS on an `insufficient_evidence` criterion (fail-closed) and its refusal message carries the INDETERMINATE remediation guidance, not a FAIL assertion; gate-behavior test.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuard/memo interaction (fix a, landed); verifier prompt changes; retry policy."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786728131970840001,"uuid":"790efd11-3319-4393-b19b-ce9e503aa8ac"}